  - `^` asserts the start of the string.
  - `\\w+` matches one or more word characters (alphanumeric and underscore).
  - `(?:-[a-zA-Z0-9]+)*` is a non-capturing group that allows zero or more hyphen followed by alphanumeric characters.
  - `:` matches the colon separating the header name and value.
  - ` .+` matches one or more spaces followed by any character.
  - `$` asserts the end of the string.
- **Matcher**: The `matches()` method checks if the entire string matches the pattern.
